    {
      "component": "Dispose and member order",
      "assessment": "Actual State retain increments before possible ownership checks, and its temporary release is always owned. Dispose clears request slot, detaches, then releases; no request or State dereference follows a potentially final release. Scope retains Environment independently through pending/error/root cleanup. Default Simple has no additional JS members; FileHandle request adds actual storage and Entry after genuine AsyncWrap init.",
      "source_ids": [
        "request_dispose",
        "simple_constructor",
        "simple_type",
        "reqwrap_constructor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "component": "StreamBase Shutdown",
      "assessment": "Stored real InstanceTemplate is used only when the native overload receives no wrapper; real Reset follows. Native callback wrapper remains held across DoShutdown/error handling. Actual stream async ID and prior default trigger are used; trigger restores before outer pointer and locals. Immediate nonzero results Dispose, error Set failure keeps UV_EBUSY and returns before ClearError. Missing actual template/virtual/environment binding is an explicit host assembly error.",
      "source_ids": [
        "stream_shutdown",
        "trigger_scope",
        "default_simple"
      ]
    },
    {
      "component": "Real FileHandle close request",
      "assessment": "FileHandleCloseWrap implements SimpleShutdownWrap<ReqWrap<uv_fs_t>> with provider35, canonical CLOSE storage and actual intrusive Entry. Closed or closing calls Done(0), returns1. Otherwise sets closing, CHECKs fd!=-1, traces and dispatches actual close; original ignored negative dispatch behavior is retained. It introduces no FileHandle Global or Promise.",
      "source_ids": [
        "filehandle_shutdown",
        "reqwrap_dispatch",
        "provider_number"
      ]
    },
    {
      "component": "Completion and callback continuation",
      "assessment": "Existing native Wrapper retains, detaches and decreases waiting before callback. Selected completion reads trace result, calls actual AfterClose, freshly reads result, cleans actual request, then Done. Completed ordinary AfterClose/listener failures are escrowed so native continuation/Dispose runs; fatal/aborted port completion performs native retirement without fabricating guest success. The outer Wrapper retains through Done. Ordinary escrow does not itself cause Scope.pending to rethrow; it observes actual current pending and returns the owned reason at finish.",
      "source_ids": [
        "filehandle_shutdown",
        "reqwrap_wrapper",
        "reporter_shutdown"
      ]
    },
